 34MG c  2013StZY: {+35}Na was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 34MG2c  345-MeV/nucleon, 70-pnA {+48}Ca{+20+} primary beam from the linear     
 34MG3c  accelerator RILAC and the four cyclotrons RRC, fRC, IRC, and SRC at    
 34MG4c  RIKEN impinging on a 15-mm-thick {+9}Be target. The secondary cocktail 
 34MG5c  beam was selected by the BigRIPS separator and the zero-degree         
 34MG6c  spectrometer (ZDS) using the B|r-|DE-ToF method, and implanted into the
 34MG7c  Cylindrical Active Implantation Target for Exotic Nuclei (CAITEN)      
 34MG8c  consisting of a segmented movable hollow-cylindrical-shaped plastic    
 34MG9c  scintillator and a stationary ring of 24 position-sensitive            
 34MGAc  photomultiplier tubes (PSPMTs) arranged on a ring inside the           
 34MGBc  scintillator at the height of the beamline. To reduce background       
 34MGCc  buildup, the scintillator barrel was rotated quickly and axially moved 
 34MGDc  slowly in vertical direction, resulting in a helix-shaped motion. |b   
 34MGEc  particles were detected by the CAITEN and |g rays were detected using  
 34MGFc  three HPGe clover detectors. Measured E|g, |b|g-coin, and implant-|b   
 34MGGc  correlation, and deduced the T{-1/2} of {+35}Na. Comparisons with QRPA 
 34MGHc  and shell-model calculations.                                          
 34MG c  2022Cr03: {+35}Na was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 34MG2c  172.3-MeV/nucleon, 120-pnA {+48}Ca{+20+} primary beam from the FRIB    
 34MG3c  linac impinging on an 8.89-mm-thick {+9}Be target. The secondary       
 34MG4c  cocktail beam centered around {+42}Si was selected by the ARIS         
 34MG5c  separator and implanted into a 5-mm-thick YSO segmented scintillator   
 34MG6c  sandwiched between two plastic scintillator veto detectors. Surrounding
 34MG7c  the implantation array were 11 HPGe clover detectors and 15 fast-timing
 34MG8c  LaBr{-3} detectors, and the VANDLE array of 88 neutron detectors. Two  
 34MG9c  Si PIN detectors and a plastic scintillator were placed 1.5 m upstream 
 34MGAc  in the last diagnostic detector box of the beamline. Ions were         
 34MGBc  identified event by event by energy loss in the upstream PIN detector  
 34MGCc  (Z determination) and time of flight between a plastic timing          
 34MGDc  scintillator at the start of stage 3 of ARIS and the timing            
 34MGEc  scintillator in the diagnostic detector box (A/Q determination) over a 
 34MGFc  flight path of 33.5 m. Measured implant-|b correlation and deduced     
 34MGGc  T{-1/2} of {+35}Na. Comparisons with QRPA and shell-model calculations.
 34MG c  1983La12, 1984La03: {+35}Na was produced via fragmentation of a 30     
 34MG2c  g/cm{+2} iridium target by 10 GeV protons from the CERN synchrotron.   
 34MG3c  The recoiling nuclear fragments were thermalized in heated graphite.   
 34MG4c  The alkali elements selectively diffused out of the target and were    
 34MG5c  surface ionized and analyzed by the online mass spectrometer, then     
 34MG6c  focused at the bottom of a well-shaped NE213 liquid scintillator       
 34MG7c  neutron detector. |b particles were detected using a well-shaped, thin 
 34MG8c  plastic scintillator. Measured |b and neutron counts. Deduced the      
 34MG9c  T{-1/2} of {+35}Na. P{-n} values were deduced for other isotopes but   
 34MGAc  not for {+35}Na.                                                       
