 34MG cG $2013StZY observed this |g ray in the background-subtracted |g-ray     
 34MG2cG spectrum in a time window of 0-10 ms after the implantation of {+35}Na 
 34MG3cG but did not observe it in later time windows. 2013StZY proposed that it
 34MG4cG could be either the deexcitation of the first 2+ level to 0+ g.s. in   
 34MG5cG {+34}Mg or the deexcitation of an excited state in {+35}Mg. Based on   
 34MG6cG theoretical calculations (2019Mo01, 2021Mi17), the |b{+-}1n should be  
 34MG7cG the dominant branch, implying that this |g ray is more likely from     
 34MG8cG {+34}Mg.                                                               
